<title>INDIA: Indian Aluminium 1996/97 net falls.</title>
<headline>Indian Aluminium 1996/97 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>year to March 31, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	   591.9 vs   1,142.4</p>
<p>    Sales	     11,555.8 vs  11,846.1</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	4.0 vs	 4.0</p>
<p>    Other income	  99.4 vs     190.8</p>
<p>    Expenditure	8,878.2 vs   8,395.7</p>
<p>    Interest	     480.4 vs     449.0</p>
<p>    Depreciation	 394.8 vs     380.0</p>
<p>    Tax		     86.8 vs     350.0</p>
<p>Note: Indian Aluminium is the country's largest manufacturer of finished aluminium products. The company said a slowdown in the aluminium industry in 1996/97 (April-March) both in India and abroad affected all its three major segments -- alumnia refining, primary aluminium and downstream aluminium products.</p>
<p>With expanded capacities and higher utilisation, the company expects a substantial increase in volumes in all its businesses, Indian Aluminium said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
